{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the Eulerian number a(n, m).\nassert eulerian_num(3, 1) == 4\n\"\"\"\ndef eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Returns the Eulerian number A(n,m) using the recurrence relation.\"\"\"\n    if m == 0 or m == n - 1:\n        return 1\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Create a table to store computed values\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base cases\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        if i > 0:\n            dp[i][0] = 1\n            if i > 1:\n                dp[i][i - 1] = 1\n    \n    # Fill the table using recurrence: A(n,m) = (m+1)*A(n-1,m) + (n-m)*A(n-1,m-1)\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i - 1):\n            dp[i][j] = (j + 1) * dp[i - 1][j] + (i - j) * dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n    \n    return dp[n][m]"}
