{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the count of all binary sequences of length 2n such that sum of first n bits is same as sum of last n bits.\nassert math.isclose(count_binary_seq(1), 2.0, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\ndef count_binary_seq(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of binary sequences of length 2n where sum of first n bits equals sum of last n bits.\"\"\"\n    from math import comb\n    total = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        total += comb(n, k) * comb(n, k)\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to calculate the maximum aggregate from the list of tuples.\nassert max_aggregate([('Juan Whelan',90),('Sabah Colley',88),('Peter Nichols',7),('Juan Whelan',122),('Sabah Colley',84)])==('Juan Whelan', 212)\n\"\"\"\ndef max_aggregate(tuples_list):\n    # Create a dictionary to store aggregated values for each name\n    aggregates = {}\n    for name, value in tuples_list:\n        aggregates[name] = aggregates.get(name, 0) + value\n    \n    # Find the name with maximum aggregate value\n    max_name = max(aggregates, key=aggregates.get)\n    return (max_name, aggregates[max_name])"}
