{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until ith index and also including a given kth element which is after i, i.e., k > i .\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5 ], 7, 4, 6) == 11\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until i, including element at k\n    max_sum_until_i = 0\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    \n    # Calculate max increasing subsequence sum until index i\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\n        dp[idx] = arr[idx]\n        for prev in range(idx):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[idx]:\n                dp[idx] = max(dp[idx], dp[prev] + arr[idx])\n        max_sum_until_i = max(max_sum_until_i, dp[idx])\n    \n    # Add the kth element if it can extend any subsequence\n    result = max_sum_until_i\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[idx] < arr[k]:\n            result = max(result, dp[idx] + arr[k])\n    \n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until ith index and also including a given kth element which is after i, i.e., k > i .\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5 ], 7, 4, 6) == 11\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence from prefix to i, including element at k\n    dp_prefix = [0] * (i + 1)\n    dp_prefix[0] = arr[0]\n    \n    for j in range(1, i + 1):\n        dp_prefix[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[j]:\n                dp_prefix[j] = max(dp_prefix[j], dp_prefix[prev] + arr[j])\n    \n    max_ending_at_i = max(dp_prefix)\n    \n    # Find elements from i+1 to k-1 that can form increasing sequence\n    result = max_ending_at_i\n    for j in range(i + 1, k):\n        if arr[j] > max(arr[idx] for idx in range(i + 1) if dp_prefix[idx] == max_ending_at_i):\n            result += arr[j]\n    \n    # Add the kth element\n    result += arr[k]\n    \n    return result\n```"}
