{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\nassert highest_Power_of_2(10) == 8\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef highest_Power_of_2(n):\n    \"\"\"Find the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    power = 1\n    while power * 2 <= n:\n        power *= 2\n    return power\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to set the left most unset bit.\nassert set_left_most_unset_bit(10) == 14\n\"\"\"\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    # Find the position of the leftmost unset bit and set it\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Find the leftmost unset bit position\n    temp = n\n    bit_pos = 0\n    \n    # Count total bits in the number\n    total_bits = temp.bit_length()\n    \n    # Check each bit from left to right\n    for i in range(total_bits, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n    \n    # If all bits are set, set the next higher bit\n    return n | (1 << total_bits)"}
