{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum product subarray of the given array.\nassert max_subarray_product([1, -2, -3, 0, 7, -8, -2]) == 112\n\"\"\"\ndef max_subarray_product(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find the maximum product of a contiguous subarray.\"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    \n    max_prod = min_prod = result = arr[0]\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] < 0:\n            max_prod, min_prod = min_prod, max_prod\n        \n        max_prod = max(arr[i], max_prod * arr[i])\n        min_prod = min(arr[i], min_prod * arr[i])\n        \n        result = max(result, max_prod)\n    \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence of that array.\nassert max_product([3, 100, 4, 5, 150, 6]) == 3000\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_product(arr):\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    \n    n = len(arr)\n    # dp[i] stores the maximum product of increasing subsequence ending at index i\n    dp = arr[:]\n    \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n    \n    return max(dp)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/471", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the product of the array multiplication modulo n.\nassert find_remainder([ 100, 10, 5, 25, 35, 14 ],11) ==9\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef find_remainder(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"Find the product of array elements modulo n.\"\"\"\n    product = 1\n    for num in arr:\n        product = (product * num) % n\n    return product\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence of that array.\nassert max_product([3, 100, 4, 5, 150, 6]) == 3000\n\"\"\"\ndef max_product(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find maximum product of an increasing subsequence.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # dp[i] stores the maximum product of increasing subsequence ending at index i\n    dp = arr[:]\n    \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n    \n    return max(dp)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum product subarray of the given array.\nassert max_subarray_product([1, -2, -3, 0, 7, -8, -2]) == 112\n\"\"\"\ndef max_subarray_product(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find the maximum product of any contiguous subarray.\"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    \n    max_prod = min_prod = result = arr[0]\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] < 0:\n            max_prod, min_prod = min_prod, max_prod\n        \n        max_prod = max(arr[i], max_prod * arr[i])\n        min_prod = min(arr[i], min_prod * arr[i])\n        \n        result = max(result, max_prod)\n    \n    return result"}
