{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to search a string for a regex pattern. The function should return the matching subtring, a start index and an end index.\nassert find_literals('The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.', 'fox') == ('fox', 16, 19)\n\"\"\"\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef find_literals(text, pattern):\n    match = re.search(pattern, text)\n    if match:\n        return (match.group(), match.start(), match.end())\n    return None\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to get all lucid numbers smaller than or equal to a given integer.\nassert get_ludic(10) == [1, 2, 3, 5, 7]\n\"\"\"\ndef get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all Ludic numbers up to n using the sieve method.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # Take the first number as the next Ludic number\n        next_ludic = numbers[0]\n        ludic.append(next_ludic)\n        \n        # If this is the first Ludic number (1), just remove it\n        if next_ludic == 1:\n            numbers = numbers[1:]\n        else:\n            # Remove every k-th number starting from the first\n            new_numbers = []\n            for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n                if (i + 1) % next_ludic != 0:\n                    new_numbers.append(num)\n            numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to get all lucid numbers smaller than or equal to a given integer.\nassert get_ludic(10) == [1, 2, 3, 5, 7]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all ludic numbers up to n using the ludic sieve algorithm.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # The first number is always ludic\n        first = numbers[0]\n        ludic.append(first)\n        \n        if first == 1:\n            # Special case for 1, just remove it\n            numbers = numbers[1:]\n        else:\n            # Remove every first-th number starting from the first occurrence\n            new_numbers = []\n            for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n                if (i + 1) % first != 0:\n                    new_numbers.append(num)\n            numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to search a string for a regex pattern. The function should return the matching subtring, a start index and an end index.\nassert find_literals('The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.', 'fox') == ('fox', 16, 19)\n\"\"\"\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef find_literals(text, pattern):\n    \"\"\"Search for a regex pattern in text and return match, start, and end indices.\"\"\"\n    match = re.search(pattern, text)\n    if match:\n        return (match.group(), match.start(), match.end())\n    return None\n```"}
