{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find nth bell number.\nassert bell_Number(2) == 2\n\"\"\"\ndef bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the nth Bell number using dynamic programming with Bell triangle.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    bell = [[0 for i in range(n+1)] for j in range(n+1)]\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i+1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i][j-1]\n    \n    return bell[n][0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/610", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function which takes a list and returns a list with the same elements, but the k'th element removed.\nassert remove_kth_element([1,1,2,3,4,4,5,1],3)==[1, 1, 3, 4, 4, 5, 1]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef remove_kth_element(lst, k):\n    \"\"\"Remove the k'th element from the list (1-indexed).\"\"\"\n    if k <= 0 or k > len(lst):\n        return lst[:]\n    return lst[:k-1] + lst[k:]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function which given a matrix represented as a list of lists returns the max of the n'th column.\nassert max_of_nth([[5, 6, 7], [1, 3, 5], [8, 9, 19]], 2) == 19\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_of_nth(matrix, n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the maximum value in the nth column of the matrix.\"\"\"\n    return max(row[n] for row in matrix)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find nth bell number.\nassert bell_Number(2) == 2\n\"\"\"\ndef bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the nth Bell number using dynamic programming.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Create triangle to store Bell numbers\n    bell = [[0 for i in range(n+1)] for j in range(n+1)]\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        # First number in each row is same as last number in previous row\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        \n        # Fill remaining entries in current row\n        for j in range(1, i+1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i][j-1]\n    \n    return bell[n][0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function which given a matrix represented as a list of lists returns the max of the n'th column.\nassert max_of_nth([[5, 6, 7], [1, 3, 5], [8, 9, 19]], 2) == 19\n\"\"\"\ndef max_of_nth(matrix, n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the maximum value in the nth column of the matrix.\"\"\"\n    return max(row[n] for row in matrix)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function which takes a list of lists, where each sublist has two elements, and returns a list of two lists where the first list has the first element of each sublist and the second one has the second.\nassert merge([['x', 'y'], ['a', 'b'], ['m', 'n']]) == [['x', 'a', 'm'], ['y', 'b', 'n']]\n\"\"\"\ndef merge(lst):\n    \"\"\"Transforms list of pairs into pair of lists with first and second elements.\"\"\"\n    first_elements = [pair[0] for pair in lst]\n    second_elements = [pair[1] for pair in lst]\n    return [first_elements, second_elements]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function which takes a list of lists, where each sublist has two elements, and returns a list of two lists where the first list has the first element of each sublist and the second one has the second.\nassert merge([['x', 'y'], ['a', 'b'], ['m', 'n']]) == [['x', 'a', 'm'], ['y', 'b', 'n']]\n\"\"\"\ndef merge(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"Returns two lists: first elements and second elements of each sublist.\"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return [[], []]\n    \n    first_elements = [sublist[0] for sublist in list_of_lists]\n    second_elements = [sublist[1] for sublist in list_of_lists]\n    \n    return [first_elements, second_elements]"}
