{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the median of two sorted lists of same size.\nassert get_median([1, 12, 15, 26, 38], [2, 13, 17, 30, 45], 5) == 16.0\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef get_median(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"Find the median of two sorted lists of same size.\"\"\"\n    merged = []\n    i = j = 0\n    \n    while i < n and j < n:\n        if list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            merged.append(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged.append(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n    \n    while i < n:\n        merged.append(list1[i])\n        i += 1\n    \n    while j < n:\n        merged.append(list2[j])\n        j += 1\n    \n    return (merged[n - 1] + merged[n]) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the median of two sorted lists of same size.\nassert get_median([1, 12, 15, 26, 38], [2, 13, 17, 30, 45], 5) == 16.0\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef get_median(list1, list2, n):\n    # Merge the two sorted lists and find the median\n    merged = []\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    \n    while i < n and j < n:\n        if list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            merged.append(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged.append(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n    \n    while i < n:\n        merged.append(list1[i])\n        i += 1\n    \n    while j < n:\n        merged.append(list2[j])\n        j += 1\n    \n    return (merged[n - 1] + merged[n]) / 2.0\n```"}
