{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWe say that an element is common for lists l1, l2, l3 if it appears in all three lists under the same index. Write a function to find common elements from three lists. The function should return a list.\nassert extract_index_list([1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7])==[1, 7]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef extract_index_list(l1, l2, l3):\n    # Find elements that are the same at the same index across all three lists\n    result = []\n    min_len = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n    for i in range(min_len):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            result.append(l1[i])\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWe say that an element is common for lists l1, l2, l3 if it appears in all three lists under the same index. Write a function to find common elements from three lists. The function should return a list.\nassert extract_index_list([1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7])==[1, 7]\n\"\"\"\ndef extract_index_list(l1, l2, l3):\n    \"\"\"Return elements that appear at the same index in all three lists.\"\"\"\n    result = []\n    min_length = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n    for i in range(min_length):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            result.append(l1[i])\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/758", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to count lists within a list. The function should return a dictionary where every list is converted to a tuple and the value of such tuple is the number of its occurencies in the original list.\nassert unique_sublists([[1, 3], [5, 7], [1, 3], [13, 15, 17], [5, 7], [9, 11]] )=={(1, 3): 2, (5, 7): 2, (13, 15, 17): 1, (9, 11): 1}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef unique_sublists(lst):\n    \"\"\"Count occurrences of sublists by converting them to tuples.\"\"\"\n    result = {}\n    for sublist in lst:\n        key = tuple(sublist)\n        result[key] = result.get(key, 0) + 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/758", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to count lists within a list. The function should return a dictionary where every list is converted to a tuple and the value of such tuple is the number of its occurencies in the original list.\nassert unique_sublists([[1, 3], [5, 7], [1, 3], [13, 15, 17], [5, 7], [9, 11]] )=={(1, 3): 2, (5, 7): 2, (13, 15, 17): 1, (9, 11): 1}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef unique_sublists(lst):\n    \"\"\"Count occurrences of sublists by converting them to tuples.\"\"\"\n    result = {}\n    for sublist in lst:\n        tuple_key = tuple(sublist)\n        result[tuple_key] = result.get(tuple_key, 0) + 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to count the pairs of reverse strings in the given string list. \nassert count_reverse_pairs([\"julia\", \"best\", \"tseb\", \"for\", \"ailuj\"])== 2\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list):\n    \"\"\"Count pairs where one string is the reverse of another.\"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    pairs = 0\n    \n    for string in string_list:\n        reversed_string = string[::-1]\n        if reversed_string in seen and reversed_string != string:\n            pairs += 1\n        elif reversed_string in seen and reversed_string == string:\n            continue\n        else:\n            seen.add(string)\n    \n    return pairs\n```"}
