{"task_id": "Mbpp/784", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the product of first even and odd number of a given list.\nassert mul_even_odd([1,3,5,7,4,1,6,8])==4\n\"\"\"\ndef mul_even_odd(nums):\n    \"\"\"Find the product of first even and odd number in the list.\"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n    \n    for num in nums:\n        if num % 2 == 0 and first_even is None:\n            first_even = num\n        elif num % 2 == 1 and first_odd is None:\n            first_odd = num\n        \n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n    \n    return first_even * first_odd"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/785", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to convert tuple string to integer tuple.\nassert tuple_str_int(\"(7, 8, 9)\") == (7, 8, 9)\n\"\"\"\ndef tuple_str_int(tuple_string):\n    \"\"\"Convert a string representation of a tuple to an integer tuple.\"\"\"\n    # Remove parentheses and split by comma, then convert to integers\n    clean_string = tuple_string.strip(\"()\")\n    if not clean_string:\n        return ()\n    return tuple(int(x.strip()) for x in clean_string.split(\",\"))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/784", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the product of first even and odd number of a given list.\nassert mul_even_odd([1,3,5,7,4,1,6,8])==4\n\"\"\"\ndef mul_even_odd(lst):\n    \"\"\"Find the product of first even and odd number in the list.\"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n    \n    for num in lst:\n        if num % 2 == 0 and first_even is None:\n            first_even = num\n        elif num % 2 == 1 and first_odd is None:\n            first_odd = num\n        \n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n    \n    return first_even * first_odd"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "\"\"\"\nGiven a square matrix of size N*N given as a list of lists, where each cell is associated with a specific cost. A path is defined as a specific sequence of cells that starts from the top-left cell move only right or down and ends on bottom right cell. We want to find a path with the maximum average over all existing paths. Average is computed as total cost divided by the number of cells visited in the path.\nassert maxAverageOfPath([[1, 2, 3], [6, 5, 4], [7, 3, 9]]) == 5.2\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix):\n    n = len(matrix)\n    dp = {}\n    \n    def solve(i, j):\n        if i == n - 1 and j == n - 1:\n            return (matrix[i][j], 1)\n        \n        if (i, j) in dp:\n            return dp[(i, j)]\n        \n        max_avg = float('-inf')\n        best_sum = 0\n        best_count = 0\n        \n        if i + 1 < n:\n            sum_down, count_down = solve(i + 1, j)\n            avg_down = (matrix[i][j] + sum_down) / (1 + count_down)\n            if avg_down > max_avg:\n                max_avg = avg_down\n                best_sum = matrix[i][j] + sum_down\n                best_count = 1 + count_down\n        \n        if j + 1 < n:\n            sum_right, count_right = solve(i, j + 1)\n            avg_right = (matrix[i][j] + sum_right) / (1 + count_right)\n            if avg_right > max_avg:\n                max_avg = avg_right\n                best_sum = matrix[i][j] + sum_right\n                best_count = 1 + count_right\n        \n        dp[(i, j)] = (best_sum, best_count)\n        return (best_sum, best_count)\n    \n    total_sum, total_count = solve(0, 0)\n    return total_sum / total_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to locate the right insertion point for a specified value in sorted order.\nassert right_insertion([1,2,4,5],6)==4\n\"\"\"\ndef right_insertion(arr, value):\n    \"\"\"Find the rightmost position to insert value in sorted order.\"\"\"\n    left, right = 0, len(arr)\n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if arr[mid] <= value:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid\n    return left"}
